-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS BUNDLED IN RELEASES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The desktop build and the Docker image bundle the following third-party
components. They are redistributed under their own terms, reproduced below.


FFmpeg  (https://ffmpeg.org/)
  License:  GPL-3.0-or-later
  Upstream source: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg
  Binary builds:  https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases

  Static builds are produced by BtbN with --enable-gpl, which makes the result
  GPL-licensed rather than LGPL. BtbN publishes the complete corresponding
  source for every build alongside each release.

  The exact FFmpeg commit corresponding to any shipped binary is recorded in
  ffmpeg/PROVENANCE.txt inside the release bundle, written automatically by
  packaging/fetch_ffmpeg.py. It reads the commit out of `ffmpeg -version`, so
  it cannot drift from the binary that is actually shipped:

      ffmpeg build   N-127507-g24e860f6d3-20261013
      ffmpeg commit  24e860f6d3
      sha256         68a315dd...

  FFmpeg's own COPYING is available at:
      https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/master/COPYING

  FFmpeg is invoked by MediaGrab as a separate executable process; it is not
  linked into the MediaGrab source.


Deno  (https://deno.com/)
  License:  Apache-2.0
  Source:   https://github.com/denoland/deno
  Binary:   https://github.com/denoland/deno/releases/latest

  Required by yt-dlp to solve YouTube's player challenge; see
  app/services/js_runtime.py. Apache-2.0 is compatible with GPL-3.0.


yt-dlp  (https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp)
  License:  Unlicense (public domain)
  Source:   https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp


yt-dlp Android  (https://github.com/ytdl-org/youtubedl-android)
  License:  GPL-3.0
  Source:   https://github.com/ytdl-org/youtubedl-android

  Applies to the Android client (MULTI_PLATFORM_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md,
  Milestone 4). Not currently shipped.


